{
  "A bar of commands: buttons, toggle buttons, menus and fields in groups between separators. It is one Tab stop and the arrow keys move inside it; items that do not fit move into a “more” menu at the end. Items come as data, as JSX children, or both.": "",
  "`items` describes the commands as data, each field a value or a function; JSX children (any control) come after them. Programmatically, a toolbar is filled like any control: `toolbar.controls.add(button)`. Every prop is also a property.": "",
  "An editor toolbar": "",
  "Filled programmatically": "",
  "Toggle groups and separators": "",
  "A `toggle` item is a toggle button (`aria-pressed`). Bound to the app with a function, it shows the app’s state: Bold, Italic and Underline above are three independent toggles, the alignment buttons a group where one is pressed. `separator` items (or `<ToolbarSeparator />`) draw the lines between groups.": "",
  "Overflow": "",
  "With `overflow` set to `menu` (the default) the items that do not fit move into a “more” menu at the end, from the last one back; the toolbar watches its own size. There they keep their names (an icon-only button its `hint` or `aria-label`), a toggle becomes a check item and a menu button a submenu. An item’s `overflow` says `always` or `never`; fields stay in the bar. `wrap` starts a second row, `scroll` lets the bar scroll.": "",
  "Orientation, size, fields": "",
  "`size` and `buttonVariant` reach the controls inside that have none of their own. A vertical toolbar moves with Up and Down. A text field inside keeps the arrow keys for its text.": "",
  "Into the toolbar, to the control used last; Tab again leaves it.": "",
  "The next / previous control, wrapping around (Left / Right in a right-to-left page). Down / Up when vertical.": "",
  "The first / last control.": "",
  "The arrows, Home and End move in the text; Tab leaves.": "",
  "Opens its menu (horizontal toolbar).": "",
  "`role=\"toolbar\"` with `aria-orientation`, named by `label`.": "",
  "One Tab stop: the control used last has `tabindex=\"0\"`, the others `-1` (roving tabindex).": "",
  "`role=\"separator\"`, turned across the toolbar.": "",
  "Toggle items are buttons with `aria-pressed`.": "",
  "A menu button named from `uiLocale` (“More options”); the items keep their names (an icon-only button its `hint` or `aria-label`), toggles become check items, menu buttons submenus.": "",
  "The only text a toolbar writes itself is the name of its “more” button, from `uiLocale.strings.moreOptions`.": "",
  "The toolbar. `data-orientation`, `data-size`, `data-overflow`, `data-disabled`.": "",
  "A separator.": "",
  "The “more” button (a `Button` with a menu).": "",
  "On a control that is in the “more” menu now.": "",
  "The bar’s least height (the density-aware bar height).": "",
  "Units: the bar (`vertical`: a column of controls) and the separators across it.": "",
  "Items as data, drawn before the JSX children (see Items).": "",
  "Names the toolbar for screen readers (`aria-label`). The same property as `text`.": "",
  "Which way it runs; the arrow keys follow it.": "",
  "Given to the controls inside that have no `size` of their own.": "",
  "Given to the buttons inside that have no `variant` of their own.": "",
  "`menu`: what does not fit goes into a “more” menu at the end; `wrap`: a second row; `scroll`: the bar scrolls.": "",
  "`enabled={false}` disables every control inside.": "",
  "ToolbarItem": "",
  "Default `'button'`.": "",
  "The caption (`&Bold` is an access key), an icon, a tooltip. A button with only an icon is named by its `hint`.": "",
  "A toggle’s state. As a function the item follows the app: its `click` changes what it reads.": "",
  "Dimmed, or left out.": "",
  "The commands of a `menu` item: submenus, check and radio items, shortcuts.": "",
  "Whether it may move into the “more” menu; wins over the toolbar. A JSX child says it with `data-overflow`.": "",
  "Pressed, in the bar or in the “more” menu. `e`: `{ item, source, event }`.": "",
  "The controls in the “more” menu now.": "",
  "The control made for an item of `items`.": "",
  "Works out again what fits, e.g. after a control changed its width.": "",
  "Your items may be plain or reactive; the toolbar reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. The list and each item's fields are read again; the controls made for items that stay are kept.": "",
  "Focuses the control Tab reaches.": "",
  "An item of `items` was pressed, after its own `click`. `e`: `{ item, source, event }`.": ""
}
